hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15855","Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Mustalim ibn Said informed us: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he intended a raid, I and a man of my people, and we had not embraced Islam. We said: We are ashamed that our people witness a battle we do not witness with them. He said: Have you two embraced Islam? We said: No. He said: We do not seek the help of polytheists against polytheists. He said: So we embraced Islam and witnessed it with him. I killed a man and he struck me a blow, and I married his daughter after that, and she would say: May you not lose a man who adorned you with this sash. And I would say: May you not lose a man who hastened your father to the Fire."
